# shir_nodes/affix_strip.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# AffixStrip: single-occurrence affix removal (Go strings.TrimPrefix /
# strings.TrimSuffix over arbitrary words; bash ${s#p} / ${s%p}).
#
# GENERIC (any frontend lowering affix strips on non-named operands).
# text is any expression evaluating to a string; pattern is the affix
# to strip (stringified like the host). When the affix is present it
# is removed ONCE; otherwise the text flows through unchanged.
# prefix=true strips a LEADING affix, false a TRAILING one.
#
# Backends: Perl index()/substr(), JS startsWith/slice,
#           C strncmp/memcmp loop, Rust strip_prefix/strip_suffix

# RESOLVED — `affix_strip_sound` is the node's own contract: one occurrence is removed
# when present (`has_affix`), the text flows through unchanged when not, the empty
# pattern is the identity on both ends, and the removed bytes are exactly the pattern
# (so the result is shorter by `length p` exactly when something was removed).
# PREFIX ARM (`${s#p}`): TextOps#strip_pre_is_the_node — the node's drop-the-literal arm
# IS the shortest-match strip of the glob `p*`, proved over the fragment matcher:
# `strip_pre [PLit p, PStar] t = affix_strip_node t p True`, with the miss arm being the
# identity (`${s#nomatch}` is `s`, not `[]`).
# SUFFIX ARM (`${s%p}`): TextOps#strip_suf_is_the_node — the mirror law
# `strip_suf [PStar, PLit p] t = affix_strip_node t p False`, the shortest matching suffix.
# SHORTEST, not greedy: TextOps#strip_pre_shortest / #strip_suf_shortest — a longer match
# never removes less, so `${s##p}` (the longest-match variant) is deliberately NOT this
# node; TextOps#greedy_star_is_not_the_node refutes the `#*`-is-empty reading and
# #whole_match_is_not_the_node refutes the pattern-must-match-the-whole-text reading.
# BOUNDARY: the pattern is the literal fragment of ShIR_TextOps_Glob (PLit, and the
# `p*`/`*p` shapes built from it). Classes, ranges, negation, extglob, brace alternation
# and quoting are outside the model — no theorem here covers them.
spec: TextOps#affix_strip_sound, TextOps#glob_strip_sound, TextOps#strip_pre_is_the_node, TextOps#strip_suf_is_the_node

node AffixStrip
tag "AffixStrip"
kind expr
# the node body (fields + tag) was lost from this file at HEAD — a doc-only
# copy of cut_at.node's header, so build.rs declared no node and the
# renderer stopped compiling. Restored from the node's own doc contract:
# one occurrence of `pattern` is removed from one end of `text`
# (prefix=true → leading affix, false → trailing); no match is the
# identity.
field text: expr
field pattern: expr
field prefix: bool
